    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 10/21/22  4:31:21 AM: When machine has been off for a extended amount of time, the hydraulics bleed off and the blade lowers. When you turn it on after that, the blade automatically comes to the top of the stroke, and might seem like it hits a little hard. That is normal due to the high pressure needed to achieve moving that amount of weight. Machine has no issues and is running good.",
