    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 04/13/23  5:52:34 AM: Replaced the 3 leaking hold down cylinders. Flipped top and bottom blade around. Cleaned and stoned both blades before re-installing. Cleaned threads on all bottom blade bolt inserts. There are 2 edges left on both blades that are new. Set gap to .0015 all the way down. Adjusted the backgauge due to it being out of tolerance. It is within .010 from end to end. Greased machine. Blew out the oil cooler and fans. Got all done and ran multiple test pieces of 22ga. Burr is good all the way down and parts are within tolerances. | Joshua Patton - 03/15/23  8:37:18 AM: spoke with David about this issue and he is going to get with Debbie to see if were going to replace all the plungers or just a few of them | Preston Ellexson - 03/15/23  4:22:54 AM: Got with James on this. He said he is having to clean every morning. His parts do start getting oil on them before the day is out. I will get with David and see how many he wants to buy. Might not be a bad idea to buy all new. I will at least order the 3 to repair these.",
    "attachments": []
  },
