  {
    "equipment_id": "1633",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1633",
    "equipment_name": "TruLaser 2030 (WC 2001)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "10659",
    "date_notified": "03/06/2024",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "Cumulative error of cooling unit E102.6 (02A5).",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "5500",
    "labor_time": "10",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Johnson Heat & Air",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "03/20/2024 10:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/28/24  6:34:18 AM: Got the contactor in on 3/18. Swapped out and let Johnson Heat & Air know. Ran machine but kept getting an LP error on the cooling unit. 3/20 I got in touch with the manufacturer and had one of their techs call to help with the remainder of the freon charge. Johnson Heat & Air came out and followed his prodcedure. They finally got the system fully charged with freon. We have been running good since with no more cooling unit errors. | Preston Ellexson - 03/14/24  7:58:28 AM: Got the compressor in. Johnson Heat & Air came out and did the swap. He needed it turned on to complete the filling of freon. Machine is still giving us the same issue. We swapped the circuit breaker that controls compressor 1 and 2. Same result that is tripping. I looked further and found the contactor for compressor 2 was engaged with no power. Released with a screwdriver, so I could tell the points were more than likely welded together. Removed wires so I could remove contactor. All points are burned up. This contactor can't be fully taken apart, or I would clean and put back together. Got one ordered from Grainger that'll be here tomorrow. When it arrives, I'm getting with Mark so they can come back out and top off the freon when I'm done. | Preston Ellexson - 03/07/24  8:41:46 AM: Compressor was just ordered overnight delivery. It'll be Monday more than likely before I can get it scheduled to be swapped out. I am going to check the circuit breaker that controls that to ensure it is still functioning properly. | Preston Ellexson - 03/07/24  5:08:07 AM: Checked error messages on cooling unit and in cabinet. CB4 circuit breaker is tripped and keeps tripping. That runs compressor 2 for the cooling unit. Checked the compressor, and it is overheating by 30-50 degrees in comparison to compressor 1. We left the machine off, and left the cover off the compressors overnight. Started the machine up this morning, and the same issue without the compressor running for 12+ hrs. Awaiting response from Trumpf on part to order. Scheduling service tech to remove and replace the compressor when it arrives.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1633",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1633",
    "equipment_name": "TruLaser 2030 (WC 2001)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "11797",
    "date_notified": "05/22/2024",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "the nitrogen generator was leaking water from the filter (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "1",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "05/29/2024 08:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 05/29/24  5:58:03 AM: This is because the front compressor room was overheating, and tripping the dryer. The black is the moisture and carbon content that's not clean anymore. Nothing to worry about just need to maintain better. | Preston Ellexson - 05/24/24  8:42:33 AM: Got the scissor lift and shut off air valve in ceiling to the nitrogen system. Drained bulk tank with water hose. Removed all air from compressor tanks, and bulk tank. Removed filter housing and element. Everything was pretty black. Still watery but very dirty. I washed and cleaned the filter element. Cleaned the housing. Put all back together, shut all tank valves, and turned air back on. No leaks right now, and no build up yet. Got with our compressor tech to see what he thinks about this. I will update when he gets back in touch.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1633",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1633",
    "equipment_name": "TruLaser 2030 (WC 2001)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "11999",
    "date_notified": "06/06/2024",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "having air issues on the laser (Preston knows about the issue) it was the suction cups",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "0.5",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "06/06/2024 02:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 06/07/24 12:17:55 PM: Replaced 2 bad suction cup pads with new. Didn't have the swivel fittings, so we used the old ones. Straightened the end mounting bracket on the load table. It was bent and causing one or two pads to not be able to work. After we swapped and adjusted the mounting bracket, I had him run the machine. We aren't getting them all to work still, but we gained 7-8psi by replacing just 2. That is enough to not shut the machine down. I am getting a quote for new suction cup pads. Machine is running good.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1633",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1633",
    "equipment_name": "TruLaser 2030 (WC 2001)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "11955",
    "date_notified": "06/05/2024",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "the tanks for the new nitrogen system need to be anchored",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
