    "problem": "Laser throwing error codes for Tasc 3 laser control in error condition, safety or motor circuit-breaker for 230V have been tripped, link to generator 1 faulty",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "700",
    "labor_time": "4",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "03/27/2025 02:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/28/25 12:28:33 PM: Got the right fan in. Installed it, mounted circuit board back. Plugged back in all wires. Turned machine on and made sure breaker was good. Took a little while to warm up after being down for over a week. Machine is running good with no issues. | Preston Ellexson - 03/24/25  7:57:50 AM: After working back and forth with Michael@Trumpf, we finally got to what he believes the issue is. There was a circuit breaker tripped inside the machine. He had me disconnect the harness that goes to the fan inside the rf generator electrical cabinet. Turned breaker back on, and now it isn't tripping. With the fan harness plugged in, the circuit breaker trips automatically. He got me the part #, and we got one ordered overnight Friday so it should arrive today. I'll install, rewire, and remount everything when it arrives. | Preston Ellexson - 03/20/25 10:42:11 AM: Tried cycling the machine power twice with no change in error status. Visually inspected the 2 main electrical cabinets and didn't see anything obvious. Reset a drive with no change. Emailed Michael@Trumpf and am awaiting a response.",
    "attachments": []
  },
