    "completed_datetime": "06/16/2025 07:30 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 06/16/25  5:55:49 AM: Machine was too low on water to find the leak. Filled tank with DI water. Turned machine back on. Found water leak. Held it tight while Vern shut the machine down. Cut bad spot out and put in a push to connect fitting. 8mm line on the back left of the entire head enclosure. No covers needed to be removed to find this, but I didn't know that when we first went over. Got covers put back on. Cleaned up as much water as we could. Turned machine back on. Checked for water leaks and everything is good now. Put the bellow back on to the enclosure. Machine is ready to run.",
