    "completed_datetime": "07/28/2026 09:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 08/12/26 11:28:40 AM: I wrapped the piping with FlexSeal. It hasn't been leaking at all anymore. I've had it on for a little over 2 weeks with no dripping. | Preston Ellexson - 05/28/26  4:40:39 AM: Got with Matthew John on this to see what kind of leak it was. Visually inspected and the fitting that is leaking is PVC, or CPVC. Shouldn't be too hard to change out, but it's all glued and there are some threaded fittings as well. I am going to take some measurements today. I will get with Shacole now I know the location. | Preston Ellexson - 05/12/26  5:09:59 AM: Got with Shacole on this. I should be able to get this looked at and possibly repaired this week. It just depends on where the leak is.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1633",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1633",
    "equipment_name": "TruLaser 2030 (WC 2001)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "20168",
    "date_notified": "07/30/2026",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "Laser is throwing a Task 3 laser error for the cooling unit and will not run. (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "3",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
