  {
    "equipment_id": "5340",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 5340",
    "equipment_name": "TruMatic 6000",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "12551",
    "date_notified": "07/26/2024",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "sheet master unlevel throwing error code. and light sensor 1 tripped (Preston working on)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "8",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "07/25/2024 02:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 07/29/24  5:36:31 AM: Worked on this 7/24 and 7/25. Had to get with Darrick@Trumpf on this. There are 2 sensors catty corner from each other on the sheetmaster. Sensor 2 is towards the front left and sensor 1 is towards the back right. Checked both. Sensor 1 is green, and 2 is green and orange. You have to teach this sensor a different height so it will allow for the material to be slightly out of level. Trumpf uses a 4mm wrench to adjust the gap. The initial distance is approx. 2.5-3mm so giving that extra 1mm is within tolerance and won't mess the machine up. Downloaded the sensor pdf to re-teach it. Took a few tries, but got this adjusted and finally got the sheetmaster raised up. Had Shacole run a few sheets to see if the issue would  happen again. All was good. End of 7/24, the skid ran out of material. When the sheetmaster attempted to pick up nothing, it was unlevel again. We got back on this 7/25. I didn't reset the sensor height. I put a bigger wrench in to get the sensor in green, raised the sheetmaster, and removed the wrench. Once raised and wrench removed, it leveled out and both sensors were back in green. Got more material loaded and started program with no issues. Removed some water from the internal chiller unit because I slightly overfilled it while I was here. Machine ran good after all this. Still monitoring this week.",
    "attachments": []
  },
