  {
    "equipment_id": "5340",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 5340",
    "equipment_name": "TruMatic 6000",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "15453",
    "date_notified": "04/22/2025",
    "urgency": "3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",
    "problem": "the safety switch for the door needs to be adjusted, it keeps throwing an alarm and MJ has to push the door in to make it run (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "1",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "04/24/2025 02:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 04/24/25 11:57:00 AM: Laser has been running good with no more sensor issues on the front doors. | Preston Ellexson - 04/23/25  4:47:38 AM: Still having issues with this. Removed the shims I put in yesterday. The mount for the actual sensor has slotted mounting holes. I loosened the 4 nuts and shifted the sensor bracket closer to the switch latch. Tightened lock nuts and tested. Safety switch is making much better now. I couldn't push the door enough to make it unlatch. I'll monitor this today with operator. | Preston Ellexson - 04/22/25 11:49:31 AM: The corner of the right door looks a little bent in. Pulled it back straight. Removed the horizontal latch for the door switch. Added a small washer to shim each bolt to get the plate closer to the safety switch. Tightened back up and laser is good to run. Matthew John is going to let me know if he has any more issues. I'll leave open until Friday unless it continues to error out on him. | Preston Ellexson - 04/22/25  6:33:04 AM: I am getting with Matthew John on this shortly. Seems the switch isn't fully engaging all the time. I'll see what I need to do to fix this .",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "5340",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 5340",
    "equipment_name": "TruMatic 6000",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "17904",
    "date_notified": "12/10/2025",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "error coming up pump high pressure, it is letting us run. (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "13",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "12/22/2025 09:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 12/22/25  7:47:09 AM: We ordered 2 new filters. Got them in Saturday. It is a different style filter, so we checked with tech support first. Swapped out the filters and filled the new one with DI. Turned machine on and we are not leaking anywhere. Let machine warm up. No errors at all are popping up. Machine is running good with no issues at all. I taped up the box with the extra filter, labeled it, and put it in the cabinet inside the machine. | Preston Ellexson - 12/19/25  5:05:21 AM: Tech support got back. I removed the filter housing and filter element. It was black and slimy. Looks like oil, but the tech said algae and slime might look like that being so dirty. Cleaned the filter with low pressure water. There wasn't any hard build-up on it. Filled the filter and housing with DI water and put it back on the machine. Turned machine power on and cycled the pump. Had Matthew John try running a program. Ran half a sheet with the pump pressure high error in yellow, then it turned to red. Machine will not run until we get a new filter, and possibly do a full water change. Filter was ordered yesterday, so it should be here Monday. I'll replace when it arrives and test the machine. | Preston Ellexson - 12/18/25 10:22:59 AM: We've been working with tech support on this issue. Found the fan for the chiller was in reverse rotation. Got that swapped. Had Johnson's Heating & Air here to check the compressor. Had them make sure it was running good and had enough freon. Compressor is good. Still getting a high pump pressure. Tech support says it might just be a filter. It is past due for the PM on this from Trumpf. Shacole let Paul know we need to schedule it. We are awaiting tech support to clarify the tech guide they sent. Doesn't match our machine. Once they reach out, we'll clean the filter if possible and see if the issues continue. Right now it won't run due to the pressure issue.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "5340",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 5340",
