  {
    "equipment_id": "5340",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 5340",
    "equipment_name": "TruMatic 6000",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "18650",
    "date_notified": "03/04/2026",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "check sensors on machine",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "2",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "03/16/2026 10:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/17/26  5:23:19 AM: Tech came out and got the laser running. It was just a reset that needed to be done. Not sure why the tech didn't tell Shacole this, but we know now. | Preston Ellexson - 03/13/26  8:03:16 AM: I did not proceed with the information below. We already had a part expedited from Germany. When the relay arrived, I swapped it out and rewired everything. Set the dip switches as well. We are getting different machine errors now, and the relay is showing different errors too. Shacole got back with Trumpf on this case. Tech said it was to the point we should get someone in here. I am leaving this open to document all findings, but I am not doing anything with this until then. | Preston Ellexson - 03/09/26 12:05:23 PM: Shacole sent me all the information from the tech support last week. We are awaiting the part they think will fix this. It is coming from Germany, so it might be a couple days. I am going to go through all the conversations with Trumpf from her tomorrow morning just to ensure we're not missing something else. There are multiple things on the machine to check that I want to verify while it's already down.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "5340",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 5340",
    "equipment_name": "TruMatic 6000",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "18705",
    "date_notified": "03/11/2026",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "Nitrogen Generator is down",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "8",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/General Compressor Inc.",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "03/19/2026 08:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/20/26  5:34:25 AM: Zach called Wednesday morning and said the pump was there. He sent Aaron here to swap everything out. He got done around 2. We got everything ready, except for the covers. Once air was built up in the system, we started the compressor. It was a bit noisy when starting, but is running good now. Everything is working as it should. I came in Thursday morning and got all the covers back on it. Double checked everything and found no issues. Cleaned a little oil from under the reservoir. It's not leaking, it's just residual from when Aaron filled it. Started compressor and let operators know it was back up and running. | Preston Ellexson - 03/13/26  8:06:47 AM: Quote was received and processed with rush delivery yesterday. We are awaiting tracking still, but we expect it will be here by Tuesday 3/17. Jeremiah said they will have someone out next week when ready for swapping out the new pump with the faulty one. I will update this after we swap and try to run it. | Preston Ellexson - 03/11/26  7:52:54 AM: They were getting a stated gas error on the old laser. Checked the nitrogen generator system. The compressor was in fault mode. I cleared it, tried to start it, and it went straight to a motor overcurrent error. Removed the fan cover from the motor. It was locked up solid. The motor shaft was pretty warm too. Not too hot to hold my hand on, but irregular. I locked out the machine and removed the covers from the air end housing. Removed motor housing mounting bracket bolts and released belt tension. When I got the belts loose and free, the motor spins free with no issues. The air end is completely locked up. Checked the electrical cabinet for any issues and found none. All fuses, relays, and components are working the way they should. Tried running the machine after removing the belts from the air end. Machine starts up and motor runs with no issues. Called General Compressor to get a tech out to inspect this. They made it out this morning. He checked everything and came to the same conclusion. He said there doesn't appear to be anything that caused it outside of the air end components. Oil is the only maintenance, and that was just completed last week. I am awaiting a quote for repair or part replacement.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "5340",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 5340",
