  {
    "equipment_id": "5340",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 5340",
    "equipment_name": "TruMatic 6000",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "19111",
    "date_notified": "04/15/2026",
    "urgency": "3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",
    "problem": "install new valve in laser for the suction cup issue we are having (Preston is aware and has parts)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "5",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "04/20/2026 01:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 04/21/26  6:26:01 AM: Got with Steve for valve unit addressing. Programmed new valve unit. Removed needed covers on the machine. Removed mounting bolts for valve, all air lines, and communication lines. Checked addresses on old valve just to be certain. Removed all fittings from old valve and put on the new one. Mounted valve in place with everything hooked back up. Replaced filter for suction block #44. Turned machine on and tested everything. This fixed the issue we were having with suction cups 3, 5, and 9. Suction cup 44 is still lighting up like it's not functioning 100%. Right now it isn't causing any issues at all. I will monitor with Matthew John to see if it starts causing problems. Put all covers back on the machine and it is ready for production. Working with Trumpf on RMA for the faulty valve unit. | Preston Ellexson - 04/15/26 12:12:41 PM: I need to read the manual for the programming unit. I will get this done tomorrow morning. The part is easy to swap, but I need to make sure the programming is clear. If not, I'll reach out to Steve@Trumpf.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "5340",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 5340",
    "equipment_name": "TruMatic 6000",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "18840",
    "date_notified": "03/23/2026",
    "urgency": "3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",
    "problem": "the laser is having issues with the suction cups picking up the sheet and not wanting to drop parts when its supposed to.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "4.5",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "04/24/2026 08:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 04/24/26  5:53:05 AM: I got this entered on another work order somehow. Time logged on here is separate than the other work order. | Preston Ellexson - 03/30/26 11:12:58 AM: The valve unit and programming device are both here. I got with Shacole on this and will get on it tomorrow between first break and lunch. | Preston Ellexson - 03/24/26  7:36:05 AM: Parts were ordered yesterday. One is out of stock and will be coming from Germany. They said 3-4 days for it. The other part will be here today. I'll get this swapped out 3/30 when I return. | Preston Ellexson - 03/23/26 10:29:37 AM: Matthew John was having issues with the suction cups not  releasing when they should. When the part was being removed, suction cup 3 is trying to grab the sheet of material. I put in a service case with Trumpf. Steve reached back out and gave me a few documents to go over and check. I ended up making a 6mm tubing plug. I disconnected suction cup 3 and plugged the air line. Had MJ run a sheet. It didn't have any issues now. Steve said a valve unit needed to be replaced. The one that controls suction cups 1-9. There is also a programmer you have to purchase so the unit can be addressed to the machine. The order was put in 3/20 and was placed 3/23. Pam is asking if they have any expedited options. Machine is running right now. Shacole is having issues with a few other suction cups. They are not releasing the part after it's been cut. It is dropping on the finished goods pallet instead of being placed and suction released. These are cups 1 and 2, so it follows what Steve suggested. I'll swap the valve out and re-program it when the parts arrive here.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "5340",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 5340",
    "equipment_name": "TruMatic 6000",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "19890",
    "date_notified": "06/18/2026",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "The machine experienced a crash last night, resulting in damage to the 10-station holder in the head. Preston will submit a case to Trumpf and initiate the required corrective-action process.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "20",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Saul@Trumpf",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "07/17/2026 02:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 08/12/26 11:36:27 AM: Saul came back. Found more parts that needed ordered to fix the multi-tool. We received them while he was still here. He got everything fixed and working. We have been running since with no issues again on this. | Preston Ellexson - 07/09/26 11:55:31 AM: Saul@Trumpf arrived first thing 7/7. We removed the stripper assembly to inspect everything again. He couldn't find any issues. I had some orings that I wasn't sure where they went. We got them on and re-installed the stripper housing. The error is coming and going still. He moved forward to check the alignment of the punch holder. We are out of tolerance and are in need of a new punch holder. I got the quote and got one coming overnight. It should be here today. He got the machine to a point where it can run. The alignment will cause slight wear on the tooling until punch holder is replaced and aligned afterwards. He was still having trouble with the multi tool. The multi tool lock isn't hitting it's up sensor. He ran out of time to get this functional. I need to removed the stripper housing and try to get it aligned up tomorrow. If I can get the multi tool to lock and unlock as it should, the machine should be able to run production. Not sure until I get into it again. I'll update this tomorrow after my findings. | Preston Ellexson - 07/09/26  7:58:17 AM: I put in a case on the Trumpf app. Steve got back with me. He had me start taking everything apart to find the visibly damaged parts. Got the stripper housing assembly removed. It needs replaced as well as the stripper ring. Everything else actually looks good still. No odd marking like it was rubbing. Steve quoted the stripper assembly that is pre-assembled for $10,200. After I sent him the pictures of damage, he said it looked like I could reuse the parts in the old one. The quote for a non-assembled stripper housing is around $5000. I got it ordered. I also requested an onsite tech just in case I got pulled away for anything else. When parts arrived, I removed all the parts from the old one. Got everything swapped out to the new housing. I had to heat up the housing due to the crash. Everything swapped out and is working manually with no issues or binding. Got the machine put all back together and powered up. Machine let me reference, but now I am getting another error. Mounting ring stripper lifting block defective. I am waiting for the tech to arrive.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "2026",
