    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 08/22/24  7:45:11 AM: Followed up after many days of running. We have had no issues with shearing parts anymore. I'm closing this out. If this issue continues when they swap to the bigger bracket/coil, I will reinvestigate the problem. As of now there are no issues with the function of the machine. | Preston Ellexson - 08/15/24 12:41:59 PM: Merritt has still been having issues with this. Swapped the AW32 oil out to AW46 this morning. He has been running all day with no issues. I am getting with him tomorrow and seeing when he is changing material to the wider brackets. I will follow-up on the work order after. | Joshua Patton - 07/11/24 12:19:34 PM: I have emailed the tech, we are having issues with Cutting shear cutting through the parts | Joshua Patton - 07/11/24  9:44:21 AM: the setup was wrong the coil on the coiltek was off center, reset up machine from the beginning and so far the machine is running parts as it should i will continue to monitor the machine before closing the work order out.",
