    "completed_datetime": "02/19/2025 07:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 02/19/25  5:03:30 AM: Checked fuses and voltage at the uncoiler. Everything is getting voltage and ready to run. Cycled machine power and started up with no issues. Shelley hasn't ran this machine in a long time, and I don't know the daily operator functions of it. Punches seem to be hitting too hard. Removed die and removed the top cylinder from the punch side. Removed the 2 shims and put back together. I wanted these the be easily removable for testing purposes. Ran a few parts then it wouldn't puncture through the material. Added the shims back on top and put some tape on them. Parts are running pretty good. Dies are a little dull and causing some rolling but they have checked QC and parts will be sufficient to run like this. No more issues right now.",
    "attachments": []
  },
