  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1967",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1967",
    "equipment_name": "Panfolder (WC#2043-M1)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "1930",
    "date_notified": "07/15/2022",
    "urgency": "3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",
    "problem": "still tripping a relay  the motor in the cabinet  getting hot you can  feel the heat coming off of it.\n we put a fan on it to keep it cool.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "24",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Mark/Jerry @ Metalforming",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "07/29/2022 03:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 08/08/22 11:19:27 AM: After adjusting one, the other motor would start overheating. He got with Kurt and found out that the right side motor is actually the main motor. The left motor is only an assist motor. After that he adjusted the brakes accordingly. He stayed while Jesse ran many parts with no issues. The machine has been in full production since Jerry left with no issues. | Preston Ellexson - 08/08/22 11:15:47 AM: Jerry left the first visit Friday 7/29/2022. He replaced the rectifier that was bad on the right motor, and replaced the brake on the left side, our right side y-axis motor. Within an hour Monday morning we were already getting alarms and the same motor overheating. He rescheduled a follow-up visit and was here Thursday 8/4/2022. Before he got here, I recorded insulation resistance on both motors. Everything was reading fine. When he got here, he started adjusting the brakes on both side. | Preston Ellexson - 08/01/22  7:32:09 AM: Got in touch with Jerry. He is working with Kurt and their team on what we should do. I am ordering new rectifiers now. He said all motors have the same one on them. I will order foot pedal switches too. Awaiting response from Metalforming. | Preston Ellexson - 08/01/22  7:30:16 AM: Found a switch that is faulty, but still operating, in the rear foot pedal that we wanted to use. After troubleshooting, he got it operational with the foot pedals swapped out. We left at 2:30, but he stayed. Called me and let me know all was good. He checked motors, checked torque values, checked graphs, ran the machine. He didn't have any errors and nothing overheating. 8/1 Jesse started getting errors around 7am. Got a list of all errors. Right y-axis motor was at 190 F. | Preston Ellexson - 08/01/22  7:21:03 AM: Jerry @ Metalforming got here 7/28. Point of view (left and right) is from our operators perspective, not the point of view intended by manufacturer. He found a bad rectifier on the left y-axis motor. When the rectifier went out, we lost the motor and brake. The right one overheated due to straining by itself to operate the ram. He found the brake was bad on the right side as well. Had to overnight for Friday. He got everything swapped out. He swapped the front and rear foot pedals. | Preston Ellexson - 07/21/22  7:04:44 AM: We have a service call scheduled for an onsite technician 8/1/2022. | Preston Ellexson - 07/19/22  4:52:40 AM: Last week machine was tripping motor starter FC06 causing an e-stop error. It is also causing 41070 error for motor temperature high. Mark added fans, but it still is giving us problems. Metalforming has been sent all information to setup a technician service call. I am awaiting availability and lead time.",
    "attachments": []
  },
