    "completed_datetime": "03/01/2023 02:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/09/23  4:34:14 AM: Machine is running good. If it errors, they call and I double check the calibration of the a-axis. Haven't had anymore issues. Germany can't do the software update until we have internet speed that is faster and more consistent. I am working with Leroy and Jeffery on this. Machine is running good though. Closing as their isn't anything else I can do aside from assist. | Preston Ellexson - 03/01/23  8:30:51 AM: I swapped the inverter cards. Ran the new left encoder cable through and soldered end on. Right side cable has no issues, so I'm not going to replace it. Machine ran for a day then started throwing errors again. AL and AR 7049. Jerry, Kurt, and factory are suggesting the drives be updated via remote. No luck today, but I am getting machine ready at end of day in hopes of Germany logging in overnight and updating. | Preston Ellexson - 02/02/23  7:08:34 AM: Machine started giving a-axis errors again. Got with Jerry at Metalforming. We ordered new encoder cables, and inverter cards per parts and tech support. They scheduled Jerry back out when parts arrive. Lead time was approximately 1 week.",
    "attachments": []
  },
