    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 11/25/24  7:19:09 AM: After working off and on with Metalforming on this issue, we found the problem. Main incoming voltage had a phase that wasn't connected anymore in the top of the disconnect. When Josh tied this in, the set screw was never tight on one of the incoming power wires. Replaced parts that were stripped out and replaced with new. Re-tapped and cleaned threads too. Got all back together. Turned breaker on and tested voltage. Everything is good now. Turned machine on and tested all axes manually. Everything is working the way it should Returned to production.",
