    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 07/22/25  4:56:55 AM: Eric said with all the upgrades, it isn't worth adding in safety mats. The original machine setup ran off a safety device and it could've been done much easier before. Now with it running off a PLC, he said it's very difficult to tie in and get the machine to function properly. They only have one other customer with aftermarket safety mats, and they hate them. The only reason they don't have them remove them is because of the downtime to do the job. I am getting with Paul today to let him know this as well. | Preston Ellexson - 05/15/25 12:31:46 PM: Next week Ishmael will be back to complete the upgrade on the older machine. I'll have him send the safety controller schematic to the factory and we'll get them installed. | Preston Ellexson - 04/14/25  8:31:13 AM: Ishmael suggested buying the safety controller module that comes with these. He said it would be easier to tie into the existing system. Schroeder can let us know where to tie in. Sent to be ordered earlier this morning. When tech arrives today I'll have them send it over for us. | Preston Ellexson - 03/24/25  7:51:08 AM: Paul got with me on this. When the techs come in to install the upgraded safety light curtains, I am going to ask them where to tie in the safety mats.",
