  {
    "equipment_id": "1967",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1967",
    "equipment_name": "Panfolder (WC#2043-M1)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "17647",
    "date_notified": "11/12/2025",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "machine is throwing faults on A axis and Y saying are not in the right position, and that A position is moving but D is not in the right position",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "0",
    "work_performed_by": "Ishmael@Metal-Forming",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "11/12/2025 02:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 11/17/25 10:10:12 AM: Got with Shacole on this. They were having an issue mainly with the D-axis. She got with Ishmael@Metal-Forming. He logged in the machine and made some slight adjustments on the D-axis. They haven't had any issues after that with this error.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1967",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1967",
    "equipment_name": "Panfolder (WC#2043-M1)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "17375",
    "date_notified": "10/20/2025",
    "urgency": "3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",
    "problem": "we have had an error multiple times today on the new folder, Error safety stop upper bar. We can clear the error and continue to run, I got in contact with one of the techs and he said it could have been the safety switch got bumped and needs to be recalibrated. I put in a request with Schroder to call me to do the calibration and the tech said he can walk us through it. I would like Preston to do the calibration on the machine when they call.",
    "status": "Closed Without Action",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "5",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Seth@Metal-Forming",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "02/09/2026 10:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 11/07/25  8:54:55 AM: I've been working with the operators in logging this error. I'm letting Seth know so he can keep this up to date with the factory. Machine is running good otherwise. Very intermittent when the error happens. Some days it won't happen all day. | Preston Ellexson - 10/24/25 11:26:46 AM: Finally got the safety stop upper bar error. Let Seth know. He had us run a couple tests. These were just on Z-axis to see where it was stopping in correlation to where it numerical says it's stopping. He did make a small adjustment. The Z was stopping slightly before hitting it's intended value. Seth said to run it like this and see if it helps out with the error at all. I will follow-up with Ken on Monday morning. I'll let Seth know any findings. | Preston Ellexson - 10/24/25  8:08:01 AM: I have been working off and on with Seth on getting this issue resolved. He is logged in on TeamViewer right now. I am going to let him know when the machine errors out so he can check some values. | Preston Ellexson - 10/24/25  5:44:42 AM: Working with Seth@Metal-Forming on this issue. He believed it might be in need of a Z-axis calibration. I checked gapping per calibration procedure. Gap is a little tight, but Seth said it might be tight for a reason. I vaguely remember Ishmael making it tighter so it would hold down our parts more consistently. It's only .21mm tighter than factory setting. Z-axis is good and doesn't need calibration. Had issues with a program yesterday. Changed over to the next job. Ken is running parts good, but still getting the safety stop upper bar error multiple times throughout the day. I am reaching out to Seth after first break to see what we should do to get this issue resolved.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1967",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1967",
    "equipment_name": "Panfolder (WC#2043-M1)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "19058",
    "date_notified": "04/10/2026",
    "urgency": "3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",
    "problem": "HAVING A ERROR POP UP CAUSING THE MACHINE TO STOP.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "4",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "05/21/2026 07:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 05/21/26  4:36:21 AM: Shacole got with Seth on this issue. He logged in and got it taken care of a couple weeks ago. I don't believe we are having any more issues with this. Last week we had one where the PLC wasn't communicating all the time. It was causing a string of errors. We had Seth log in overnight while we were gone. We haven't had any issues since. Next week we will have a tech here for the older machine. If we are having anymore issues, I can run it by them while they are onsite. | Preston Ellexson - 04/22/26  6:21:09 AM: When the tech comes to do the repair on the old panfolder, I am going to have them check these errors out. | Preston Ellexson - 04/10/26  8:57:29 AM: I got with Jesse on this. I have pictures of the errors. I sent them to Jerry@Metalforming. I am awaiting a response. I will reach out to Seth if I don't hear anything back today. Machine is still running good. No parts are being scrapped. Jesse is just acknowledging the error, continuing, and then finishing the parts. I will update this when I hear back from Metalforming.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1967",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1967",
    "equipment_name": "Panfolder (WC#2043-M1)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "19112",
    "date_notified": "04/15/2026",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "parts need to be installed on the old folder for the a axis.  (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "12800",
    "labor_time": "12",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Jesse@Metalforming",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "05/27/2026 12:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 06/05/26  5:33:56 AM: Jesse arrived 5/26 midday. Got the folding beam at 0, turned machine off, and locked out. I got 2 stacks of pallets underneath each side of the folding beam. We removed the left and right motors, spindles, spindle nuts, groove nuts, and bearings. Cleaned all the old grease from the motor housing and inside all places the parts were removed. We started putting the new parts on and in place. Got everything set pretty even left to right and slowly started re-assembling the folding beam in place. I worked one side while Jesse worked the other so it stayed even during assembly. We got all this done and completed with no issues at all. We got everything full of fresh grease. Cleaned up all pallets, tools, rags, etc. Unlocked the machine and turned the power on. We calibrated the A-axis multiple times to get the tolerance as tight as we could. Once he was ready for an operator, I left them to it. He worked with Jason while running parts to fine tune. Adjustments were made as needed for the bend angle and a-axis. He got to a point where the machine was running good parts and didn't need any more adjustments. Machine is ready to run. All parts were swapped with no issues or concerns during the repair. | Preston Ellexson - 04/21/26  8:59:25 AM: Metalforming has scheduled a tech to travel on May 26th. | Preston Ellexson - 04/21/26  6:26:41 AM: Email has been sent to Metalforming for scheduling. | Preston Ellexson - 04/16/26  4:07:13 AM: Parts are all here. I need to get with Paul on this to schedule Jerry out here.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1967",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1967",
    "equipment_name": "Panfolder (WC#2043-M1)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "19587",
    "date_notified": "05/27/2026",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "the new suction cups for the old folder will need to be put on",
    "status": "Pending",
