    "completed_datetime": "02/10/2026 01:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 02/11/26 11:22:39 AM: Inspected the charger and found no issues at all. Removed my lock, turned on power, and plugged in lift to charge. Got the thermal to inspect while charging. Negative battery cable was slowing warming up more than the positive at the connector. I went ahead and replaced the connectors on the forklift and on the battery charger. The end on the charger was cracked on both sides. By the thermal image, it looks like the connection was a little loose during charging because of this. Cables are going to get warm due to the amount of amperage they charge at. Connectors look much better now. Charger is good to use. | Preston Ellexson - 02/09/26  5:20:33 AM: Shacole got with me on this Friday just after end of shift. I had her lock this out. I have the lockout key and will be over shortly to inspect the charger and cables.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
