    "completed_datetime": "06/09/2023 08:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 06/12/23  4:16:25 AM: Removed the electrical starter box for the motor and brought to maintenance. Took apart the contactor that was believed to be faulty. Found a contact point that was melted and not repairable. Had to search for one in stock, but got one overnighted. When I got back to the machine, I wired back in the contactor. Had to adjust the timer delay. After following the electrical schematic to ensure the wiring was accurate, I tested. Found no issues and the motor is running the way it should. All voltages are good and motor is running smooth. Machine is good to run. | Joshua Patton - 05/31/23  4:04:28 AM: i believe the motor is bad, want to confirm with Preston before ordering a new one.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "246",
