    "completed_datetime": "08/16/2024 01:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 08/16/24 12:41:55 PM: Removed cover. It was pretty dirty in the corners and on the impeller blades. Cleaned all off. Motor never was heating up. Found the motor data plate was making a lot of noise due the the vibration. Removed 2 bolts that hold the dust collector outlet on. They were too long and were riding on the impeller. Got all put back together and it was dragging even when moving by hand. Put on foam sealant all the way around to gap it out a little. Tightened and tested impeller by hand. No dragging or anything. Put all back together and tested motor via controls. No issues at all. Ready to run.",
    "attachments": []
  },
