    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "the collector for the fladder overflowed with water, the operator turned the valve off for the water but he said it didn't stop the water.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "1",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Derek/Shacole/Jason/Wanda",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "11/20/2024 01:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 11/25/24  7:07:15 AM: Float on the dust collector got stuck. Machine kept filling up with water. When they turned the valve off, they also shut the machine off. Pressure is released and water level rises when the machine is turned off, so it spilled even more. Got everything cleaned up. Float is working fine, it was just extremely dirty and got stuck. Let Shacole know we should change the emergency shut down procedure moving forward. If water continues to flow, turn the valve off, but leave the dust collector running. Going to see if they want me to remove, or replace the float on the machine.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
