    "completed_datetime": "06/09/2025 07:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 06/10/25  4:07:40 AM: Operator turned motor on, and then vacuum motor on. Without turning the table on, but the table knob at 100%, the machine creates a lot more vacuum for some reason. I think this is the design. When you turn the table knob down to the normal 40%, it's quieter like normal. That is still with the table not running. I don't see any issues with this due to the fact the vacuum is like normal with the table speed lower. Operator only had it that high to clean it on Friday.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "246",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 246",
    "equipment_name": "Fladder AUT",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "15127",
    "date_notified": "03/20/2025",
    "urgency": "5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",
    "problem": "I ordered a new drive belt for the fladder, which has a 4-week lead time, I will update you when it comes in.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "12",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Dennis",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "07/15/2025 10:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 07/22/25  4:47:00 AM: Started 7/9. Cleaned machine, dust collector, and vacuum motor as best we could. Got all back inside before the end of day. Came in 7/10 and had some things to do inside. Dennis worked on fixing numerous electrical issues. Removed 120V switch for fan and he put on a plug and receptacle to be plugged in when needed. He ran new SO cord for the machine power quick disconnect due to a bare wire inside the junction. Went through the belt swap process. Cleaned the conveyor unit with wire wheels while the belt was off. Got it back on the machine. After some digging, I realized I accidentally left the top piece of the machine outside and we found out someone stole it. Had to order needed parts and get started on a replacement. Dennis got the bed level while I started this. Made a 16ga piece out of stainless steel. Had Chad help with bends and with brackets for the brushes too. Dust collector fitting came in 7/14. I finished the top machine piece end of that day. Started up 7/15 and the machine was spitting out so much dust. At the table mainly, but up top too. Checked rotation on dust collector and found it was backwards. I ran it for 30+ minutes that way so it broke up the rest of the dust inside the machine and created a mess for a little bit. Turned off breaker and swapped rotation. Let it run for 20 minutes or so and they dust subsided. Cleaned up mess on floor. Got machine and everything ready to run. Made adjustments on the belt at 100% speed while operators were setting machine up to run. Still made adjustments off an on last week. Everything else is good to run. No more issues. Bed is level and running quality parts. Operators are getting much better results than before. | Preston Ellexson - 07/03/25  8:26:29 AM: Getting with Shacole 7/7 to check weather forecast. We will determine a day then. We are going to do the cleaning PM for all while we swap the belt. | Scott Herbert - 04/15/25  8:29:55 AM: Awaiting delivery of belt.",
    "attachments": []
  },
