    "problem": "Ram bolt broke off (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "1",
    "work_performed_by": "Preton",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "05/12/2025 07:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 05/12/25  5:55:47 AM: Put adjustable die blocks under ram to hold in position. Locked machine out. One of the ram lug bolts on the right inside cap broke. The front one was only finger tight when I went to remove it. Got the cap off. Broken bolt wasn't in a place I could drill and ease out. Had to use a hammer and chisel to work the broken bolt out. Finally got it out. Replaced both bolts with new and tightened down. Checked all front ram lug bolts on both sides. Everything is tight. Removed lock and powered machine on. Removed die blocks and machine is ready to run. This will be something I add to our PM so we can start checking them more frequently.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
