  {
    "equipment_id": "247",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 247",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #46 (WC 2010)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "16459",
    "date_notified": "07/22/2025",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "one of the bolts fell out on the cylinder, operator is keeping an eye on it to make sure it doesn't move (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "4",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "07/24/2025 12:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 07/25/25 12:13:31 PM: Put die blocks in ram and hand tightened. Locked machine out. Removed the cylinder with a die cart. Removed broken bolts. Ran a tap through the cylinder threads to clean them up. Got the cylinder mounted back on the machine. Tightened all cylinder pin bolts. Checked other cylinder bolts. Checked ram lug bolts in front . Nothing else was broken or even loose. Turned machine on and removed die blocks. Everything is ready to run. | Preston Ellexson - 07/22/25 11:51:44 AM: Operator found a broken bolt on the ground. I looked at all cylinders and cylinder pin mounts. Rear right cylinder by hydraulic tank broke a bolt on the bottom of the cylinder pin housing. Shacole wants to wait til Thursday or Friday when they have a bit of free time. Shouldn't take long to remove the bolt and replace with new. I'll check rocker arm bolts, rod pin bolts, and connecting rod bolts while I'm here.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "247",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 247",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #46 (WC 2010)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "16814",
    "date_notified": "08/26/2025",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "back gauge stopped moving, error message came up.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "5",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Dennis",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "10/10/2025 02:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 10/13/25  5:51:49 AM: Got parts in and scheduled repair with Shacole. Mounted motor back on the machine and tightened. Put belt on and got the tensioner set and tightened. X-axis moves freely when manually moving. Put covers on backgauge. Removed harnesses/etc from drive. Swapped out faulty drive with refurbished drive. Plugged everything back in. Turned machine on and tested by calibrating. X-axis is moving in the opposite direction. Got with Capital 10/9 and they sent a request for tech support 10/10. Got a call just after first break. Had to get internet to the machine and get ready for tech support. Ran line from the poe switch at Shacole's desk. Took a couple tries with Teamviewer. Version on machine wouldn't connect to the internet. Ended up downloading version 13 on my computer and putting on a flash drive. Installed on the machine and it connected right away. Called Edwin back at Capital and gave him Teamviewer info. He sent to tech support. They logged in just before lunch and were troubleshooting. After lunch I went over and the backgauge was ready. No errors. Calibrated Y-axis and ran a test program. No issues at all. Cleaned all oil on top of reservoir and machine is ready to run. | Preston Ellexson - 09/30/25  9:48:58 AM: Parts will arrive this Thursday. I've already gotten with Wesley in shipping on this order. I will work with Shacole's production schedule next week to repair this. | Preston Ellexson - 08/28/25  4:22:00 AM: Inspected the machine. Removed panels for the access to both backgauge belts/motors. A nut had come loose from the left side X-axis ballscrew. Everything was still in place and functional. Put it back on and tightened. Checked right side as well. Motor/belts/pulleys all move freely on X axis. Turned machine back on and opened electrical cabinet door. Had Eddie try to calibrate while watching the backgauge. It will shift for a second then drive is showing and F. error. Left and right side ballscrews do shift slightly when trying to calibrate. This is a position or velocity following error. We had a used identical motor in maintenance. Removed cables from motor on machine and plugged this one in. Turned machine on and tried again. Same result with the same error. Got with Kirk and he figures it's the drive. I left motor off and got machine ready to run in ETS100 pedestal mode for some hem/flat operation. I manually moved the R-axis up and pushed backgauge where needed for a single brake. Soft clamped in place. I removed the motor from the backgauge next day. Removed the cables from the X-axis motor on BP#42 and put the BP#46 motor in place so I could watch the motor shaft. Had Eddie turn the machine on and try to calibrate. Motor runs smooth with no errors on the drive. It is a bad drive or cables on BP#46 after testing this. Sent in for a quote and received one before end of day 8/27. Lead time is 3 weeks. Quote was sent and approved. It should be sent to Capital today. They can continue to run the machine as is. I let them know I could re-position the backgauge if needed for single brake operations until the drive arrives.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "247",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 247",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #46 (WC 2010)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "17329",
    "date_notified": "10/17/2025",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "R Target on machine was off from what it was the day before. (Preston is aware and monitoring)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "0.5",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "10/24/2025 07:30 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 10/24/25  5:46:17 AM: Machine hasn't had any issues with R target. Calibration is working the way it should. Machine has ran good all week long with no faults. | Preston Ellexson - 10/17/25 11:40:43 AM: Got with Chad on this. When he calibrated his r-axis this morning, it was approximately 1/4\" higher than normal. He would have to adjust every program to run right. His concern was if it calibrated to the original height with another operator, it might crash into the bottom die. Everything is functioning the way it should. I will follow-up first thing Monday when they turn the machine on to see where it calibrates to. Already got with Chad and Shacole.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "247",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 247",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #46 (WC 2010)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "17525",
    "date_notified": "10/30/2025",
    "urgency": "3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",
    "problem": "back gauge is out of align (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Pending",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "0.25",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "10/31/2025 10:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 10/31/25  8:16:06 AM: Backgauge needs to be measured to see how much adjustment it needs to be straight. Hopefully it's just out of square and not damaged beyond that. If it is no longer straight, it will need to be machined or replaced. I need to schedule with Shacole. I will see if we can this this done next week before my vacation.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "247",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 247",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #46 (WC 2010)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "17371",
    "date_notified": "10/20/2025",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "the site glass for the oil you cant see where it is at, and there is a oil leak on top of the cylinder.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "6",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "03/18/2026 04:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/20/26  6:29:20 AM: Got the main gasket on 3/18. I did an oil change while I was here. Changed the return line filter. Changed the suction strainer on the pump as well. Had to wait 2 days for the strainer to arrive. Put all back together when it showed up. Got all lines and cables hooked back up. Everything is tight. Wired motor back up and insulated the lugs. Double checked everything before turning on. Cycled ram on the machine for 15 minutes with no issues. It was the end of the day, so Chad didn't have time to set-up. He got the hem/flat operation setup next morning. Machine was giving him some issues. It was bending consistently, but very slow once it grabs the material. I got with Kirk and he gave me a couple things to look at. Stopped by the machine after our meeting and it was running much better. Not sure if it was just air in the system or what. Machine is running good now with no issues. There is still a pretty good leak on top of the tank. It must be the manifold that is leaking. I didn't want to remove all the lines from the pump, so this didn't get replaced. I'll get with Shacole when she gets back 3/23 to see what we want to do moving forward. | Preston Ellexson - 10/20/25 10:23:57 AM: Neither cylinder is leaking. The seals on the tank need to be replaced. I cleaned this last week, and it's already full of oil again. Motor/pump plate has to be removed to properly replace the tank seal. Got with Shacole, and we will schedule to do this when we start the machine move in fabrication. I am going to see if I can clean the sight glass without removing it. If not, it will have to wait until we do the tank seals due to mounting access.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "247",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 247",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #46 (WC 2010)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "18864",
    "date_notified": "03/24/2026",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "foot pedal safety switch isnt engaging right",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "0.75",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "03/24/2026 10:30 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/24/26  9:34:19 AM: Turned machine off and locked out. Took apart foot pedal to repair the front stop. Nothing was broken. The spring was a little bent and not fully tensioned. Took rod out and removed spring. Straightened the coils a little bit, and stretched the spring out for more tension. Put back together and tested the foot pedal. It is working the way it should now. Put foot pedal back together and turned machine back on. Machine is good to run. Safety latch on foot pedal is working properly now.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "247",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 247",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #46 (WC 2010)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "18954",
    "date_notified": "04/02/2026",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "cylinder leaking on the brake press, shooting fluid out every time the brake press gets under pressure.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "3",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Dennis",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "04/02/2026 12:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 04/03/26 11:17:34 AM: This was the cylinder that got repaired years ago. We have a brand new cylinder here to replace this with. Locked the machine out. Got the lines off and plugged. Removed the cylinder from the machine. Put the new cylinder on and hit pins in place. Tightened bolts after they were in. When removing the fittings from the cylinder, I had an issue with the bottom one. Looks like when they welded it the threads got damaged inside. I could barely get the fitting to move; even once it was loose. I went to Jimmie's Auto Supply and bought an identical fitting. Came back and installed it. Got hydraulic lines hooked back up. Cleaned up all the oil mess on the floor and on top of the reservoir. Unlocked machine and turned on. Calibrated the machine with no issues once the fluid built up in the cylinder. Had Chad run a hem/flat part. Machine is running good. It doesn't make near as much noise as before, and doesn't seem to hit as hard. There is still leaking on top of the tank. Not sure from where. I'll get with Shacole and see what they want to do about it.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "247",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 247",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #46 (WC 2010)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "19070",
    "date_notified": "04/13/2026",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "Handle for the laser curtains broke",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "2.5",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "04/13/2026 12:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 04/13/26 11:13:54 AM: The handle on the right side light curtain broke. I tried drilling it out, using an ease out, and left handed drill bits. Nothing was removing it, and the ease outs felt like they were at the point of snapping. I removed the assembly from the machine and rested it on their yellow cart. Tried using a chisel to tap/twist it out, but still no luck. I got it loose so it would move freely up and down the track. Removed the top cover and removed the handle block with the broken stud. Took to maintenance and put in the mill. Removed as much of the handle stud as possible with a 1/4\" end mill. Tried working it around the hole to remove it. Not any luck their either. I got it thin enough with a hand file where I could start to see thread marks. Used a tapered tap and slowly cleaned the threads. Got them cleaned and usable. Put the assembly back on the machine and used a socket head allen bolt in place of the handle. After looking in maintenance, we don't have any handles for these. I am getting some ordered for backup. Light curtain is holding and working as it should. I will replaced the bolt with a handle when they arrive.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "247",
