    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "01/18/2024 11:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 01/22/24  6:36:43 AM: Something on the slide adjust wasn't working and the ram got over 1/2\" out of level. Got ram down so I could inspect. Released tensioners on left and right slide adjust chains. Removed links in both chains to get free. Unwired slide adjust motor and removed. Got out of machine and found both sprockets had loose set screws, and the shaft key had shifted off the shaft and out of the right side sprocket. Cleaned and inspected motor for any damage. All looks good and the magnetic brake is still working fully. Had to remove both sprockets with a puller. Cleaned shaft and inner sprockets so I could remove/reinstall by hand. Trimmed back all motor wires due to the length. New shaft key. Reinstalled motor and changed SO fitting. Rewired and mounted motor. Got both chains back on with tensioners set. Got ram on bottom and measured height left and right. Adjusted until level, and set indicator to correct height. Put chain back on indicator sprocket and tested machine. All is running good. New heights need to be set for all dies now unfortunately.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "242",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 242",
    "equipment_name": "Punch Press, 150 ton (WC 2005)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "8167",
    "date_notified": "11/28/2023",
