  {
    "equipment_id": "242",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 242",
    "equipment_name": "Punch Press, 150 ton (WC 2005)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "12325",
    "date_notified": "07/10/2024",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "smoke coming from top of machine",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "13765",
    "labor_time": "20",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/BCN/LMG Services/DCW",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "12/02/2024 02:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 12/09/24  5:10:08 AM: LMG never worked out for the repair. We found an out of state company that was capable of completely this. David Cooper @ DCW MFG and Industrial Services came out 11/25-11/27. Removed all wiring/boards/components that were no longer needed. Wired motor and got VFD programmed and set parameters. Found out we needed a dynamic brake on this. Had to order over Thanksgiving and come back 12/2. Installed and adjusted needed parameters. Watched machine operate and everything is working good. | Preston Ellexson - 08/22/24  7:42:50 AM: I will have to make a motor mount to fit the bigger motor on the existing plate and line it all up with the flywheel. 9/3 I have Jeff@LMG Services showing up to assist in the removal of all eddy current drive components/wiring. He will also be tying in the VFD and getting everything wired into the safety circuit,etc. | Preston Ellexson - 08/22/24  7:41:10 AM: Clutch drive up top was locked up. Worked with BCN to figure out repair options. A week or so after this happened, I went to check something on the machine. Plugged main air in, and I heard a pop come from up top somewhere. I was curious if the main Ross valve was stuck and when the machine started that day. If so, that would explain the clutch drive locking up and smoking due to the brake being engaged. This would have not allowed the flywheel to physically engage, but the drive was trying to engage it. I ordered a new valve and already got it swapped out. We are going to an upgraded version and removing the motor and eddy current drive setup. We will be going up motor sizes, and running it all off a VFD setup. Motor/inverter and shaft coupler should ship 8/26 and be here next week.",
    "attachments": []
  },
