    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 07/25/23  4:30:36 AM: Inspected the table on the machine. The covers around the turret were all loose causing them to sag. I removed 2 of the sets of roller sections on the material side of the table. Replaced any missing bolts/nuts on the covers directly around the turret and that raised it back it where it needed to be. Tested a part and one still got caught up. The middle portion of the table is bowed, and that's causing both corners to be a little bit lower than where they should be. I used a pry bar and slightly bent the edges up a little bit. Ran multiple parts on medium speed with no issues. If this continues in the future, that section of the table needs to be removed and flattened out to fix the issue.",
    "attachments": []
