    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 08/10/22 10:05:40 AM: Zero-set the machine and everything looks good. Had Jacob finish out the part they had set-up. Ran good all the way through the program. I am putting the external covers back on now and then the machine will be ready for production. | Preston Ellexson - 08/10/22 10:03:50 AM: Replaced both cam plates, camshaft, and both camshaft bearings. Replaced the toggle up and down sensors while I was here. Replaced the camshaft set screw and nut. When this is all put back together, you have to leave the cam plate bolts almost loose. If you snug them, the camshaft will eventually lock up on the cam plate and start to put unneeded pressure on the bearings. Got all parts back on the machine. Adjusted the toggle up sensor to the correct height and gap. | Preston Ellexson - 06/28/22  7:11:09 AM: There was a broken bolt in the link. The cam plates, shaft, and both bearings are no good. Awaiting a quote from Murata for cost and availability. | Preston Ellexson - 06/27/22  6:52:51 AM: Toggle Up sensor error. I am finishing up a job then heading over again.",
    "attachments": []
  },
