  {
    "equipment_id": "231",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 231",
    "equipment_name": "Forklift",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "19586",
    "date_notified": "05/27/2026",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "hydraulic hose needs to be replaced",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "46",
    "labor_time": "3",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "05/27/2026 02:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 05/27/26 12:31:56 PM: Removed leaking hose. Had to remove another hydraulic line to have wrench access on the pump side. Got it off and took to Jimmie's Auto. They made a replacement. I came back and installed it on the lift. Tightened all fittings. Tested for leaks with no issues. Sent lift back to production. Cleaned up mess. | Preston Ellexson - 05/27/26  9:34:15 AM: Side shift hose is leaking pretty bad. Cleaned underneath so the leak wouldn't continue dripping on the floor. Cleaned up all mess on the shop floor. Lift is in maintenance out of commission. I am removing the hose now and going to Jimmie's Auto Supply for a replacement.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "231",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 231",
    "equipment_name": "Forklift",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "18909",
    "date_notified": "03/30/2026",
    "urgency": "2. General Maint - High Priority",
    "problem": "The cable for the scale got split on Saturday, we wont be able to take out any scrap until fixed.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "4",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "06/08/2026 07:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 06/08/26  4:43:52 AM: I finally got this repaired with a new cable and with new fittings. Paul order 5 of each fitting because they were hard to find in stock anywhere. Everything is working good now. | Preston Ellexson - 05/06/26  6:46:40 AM: This broke again. I repaired it last week when it happened. There are 2 splices in this cable now. Our vendor is having issues getting this. I spoke with him 4/16. He let me know the manufacturer discontinued these fittings and doesn't make them or sell them anymore. He needed more information to see if he could get this taken care of. I emailed him 4/21 with the info and haven't heard anything back yet. The cable broke again yesterday in another place. I am ordering the parts elsewhere so I can get a new one made here. Cable will be here tomorrow, but not sure when the fittings will arrive. They are not from one of our vendors. I will repair this 5/8 if everything is here. If not, it'll be completed next week. | Preston Ellexson - 04/02/26  8:49:58 AM: Pam is working on getting a new cable ordered. | Preston Ellexson - 03/30/26  6:47:23 AM: Cut back both cable ends about an inch. Trimmed and stripped each side back approx. 4 inches. I wanted to use butt connectors so it would look better, but I've done that before. It pulled them right apart when the lift was raising the forks with tension on the cable. I used small wire nuts and made sure all were tight. I taped it up nicely and put a couple zip ties on it to hold in certain places. Tested and everything is working the way it should. Took lift back to fab for production. I'm ordering another one. I'll leave this open so I can note the cost and eta on it. I'll keep it on the shelf until we have issues with this one again.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
