    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 191",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #45 (WC 2011)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "14167",
    "date_notified": "12/26/2024",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "while machine was running it threw a tonnage control error. machine was shut down and restarted and it will not calibrate or ram up. Matt (guy from capitol) i had him look at it and he thinks the spider gear that was replaced may have slipped.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "40",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Matt, Thomas, Kirk @ Capital Machine",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "04/18/2025 12:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 04/22/25  5:46:10 AM: A lot of work has been done to this machine to get back up and running. New pump. New hydraulic lines inside reservoir. New oil and filter. Oil was completely drained from machine, cylinders, and hydraulic lines. New main board. New tonnage transducer. New solenoids and cable assemblies. New high pressure valve. Kirk found the issue though. I accidentally left a red hose plug in one of the lines. Turned machine on and I adjusted the ram speed. When I did, it lodged it in a needle orifice causing pressure restrictions. Kirk removed it and it is running good now. Part was ordered yesterday and will be an easy replacement when it arrives. Everything else on this machine is running good now. | Scott Herbert - 04/15/25  8:35:23 AM: Awaiting return of Capital Machinery to complete repair.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "191",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 191",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #45 (WC 2011)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "15513",
    "date_notified": "04/28/2025",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "brake press making a weird sound on start up. Preston aware.",
    "status": "Closed Without Action",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "1.25",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "05/09/2025 06:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 05/09/25  4:05:07 AM: Shifting this work order to the newer one open for the ram issue. Kirk sent me the additive to get that might help this issue. I am continuing on investigating ram issue. | Preston Ellexson - 05/02/25  5:30:05 AM: Installed sun needle valve we've been waiting for. Cleaned up all oil. Turned machine power on and started up. Start/Stopped the motor a few times before letting it run. It's still making noise. To me it doesn't sound as loud. I will monitor all day off and on to see how quiet it gets after running. Kirk said they have an additive that can sometimes help this issue. He's going to send me what they use, and he might stop by in 2 weeks on the way to a job to drop some off for us. I'm leaving this open until the issue of the motor/pump noise is resolved. | Preston Ellexson - 05/01/25  7:53:50 AM: Part arrived yesterday for this machine. Got with Shacole and I am going to get this done first thing tmrw (5/2) morning. | Preston Ellexson - 04/30/25  4:12:53 AM: I am monitoring this machine. It runs really good once it's warmed up. We are still awaiting one more part to arrive from Canada that goes in the valve. That might make a difference and might not change anything. Checking tracking on part.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "191",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 191",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #45 (WC 2011)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "15626",
    "date_notified": "05/05/2025",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "Ram went up on its own, trying to recalibrate the machine, will not calibrate.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "6",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "05/09/2025 10:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 05/22/25  6:16:46 AM: There was part of a plug inside the high volume valve. Got it all cleaned out. Replaced all needed seals. Put back on the machine and hooked everything back up. Turned machine on and calibrated with no issues. Machine is running good now. I still need to send the oil additive to be ordered but everything else is working the way it should. | Preston Ellexson - 05/08/25 11:55:05 AM: Removed high speed control and checked the needle valve I put in. Went ahead and replaced the seal. I saw a spot where it was shaved a little bit. Put back on the machine after oiling it on the inside. Removed lock out and turned machine on. Tested with no change. As soon as motor is engaged, ram starts coming up to top. Let it settle a little. Removed all hirschmann cables from valves and started. Machine still starts coming up. Called Kirk and he said take the valves off and check. He believes there is something still in the hydraulic system. I am removing the valves and going from there.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "191",
