  {
    "equipment_id": "191",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 191",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #45 (WC 2011)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "18457",
    "date_notified": "02/12/2026",
    "urgency": "3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",
    "problem": "machine is stuttering on the down stroke (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "8",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Aiden@Capital",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "03/02/2026 02:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/09/26 12:13:29 PM: Tech came out and inspected everything. He ran the machine and it started doing the same hesitations with the ram/valve. He ran through multiple tests and found no issues. He temporarily removed the LaserSafe from the machine electrical. Machine ran fine while the light curtains were bypassed. He tied back in the electrical and ran the machine for over 50 strokes with no issue. He had the operator run over 70 parts with no issues. He is thinking there was something in the hydraulic line that was causing us issues, but can't be certain. Either that or a loose electrical connection. Machine is running with no issues now. | Preston Ellexson - 02/23/26  6:28:16 AM: Started by tightening all connections inside the pedestal assembly and on the main board. Checked all fuses. Both the pedestal and foot pedal cables were loose from the fittings inside the pedestal. Some wires were damaged. I cut off about 8\" of wire and rewired everything. Checked foot pedal switches. They needed adjusted as well. Both were engaging at the same time. Checked torque on the ways and adjusted slightly. Got all ready to turn on. Calibrated with no issue, but it still isn't running right. The ram and gauge enable lights flicker constantly. Ram still doesn't engage every time the foot pedal is pressed. Kevin suggested having a tech here if we were to the point of changing the main board. We have overlay, pedestal board, main board, and more cables if needed for the repair. Tech will be here 2/25 unless something changes. | Preston Ellexson - 02/19/26  4:23:36 AM: I am working on this with tech support. They called end of the day 2/20. I am awaiting a call this morning. | Preston Ellexson - 02/12/26  5:58:10 AM: Working with tech support. The solenoid is flickering on and off as Chad completes a down stroke. Very sporadic on how often it's happening. I'm seeing what Kirk thinks. Foot pedal switches, valve sticking, circuit board issues, bad solenoid or something of that matter. I will get back on this around 9.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
