  {
    "equipment_id": "191",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 191",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #45 (WC 2011)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "19171",
    "date_notified": "04/22/2026",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "machine is shuddering when in the down stroke (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "4",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Issac@Capital",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "04/27/2026 02:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 04/30/26  5:23:31 AM: Kirk said do an oil change before scheduling a tech. Removed the old oil. Used our borescope to inspect as much of the inner tank as I could. Lovejoy coupler was still fully intact. The spider was fully intact as well. Nothing had separated, so the set screws are still tight. No loose bolts I saw and nothing looked out of the ordinary. There were some small shavings at the bottom of the tank, but that is pretty normal considering we aren't fully cleaning the oil system. Got everything cleaned up. Turned the machine on. Calibrated with no issues. Ran the program they were on. It slowly started acting up on me again. I put in an email for this to Capital. They are doing a warranty tech visit since we have already had 2 techs here for the same issue in February and March. Isaac@Capital came out and swapped the main board. That got the issue resolved. We had a board here, and I could've replaced it if they would've suggested to. Machine is running good with no issues. I'll order another board for backup. They sent a quote to repair the leak on the Wila clamping system. I will proceed with that as well. | Preston Ellexson - 04/22/26 12:21:36 PM: Operator came and told me the ram was doing its hesitation again. Turned power off to the machine. Checked all harness connections in the electrical cabinet and in the LaserSafe electrical cabinet. Checked all relays. Nothing appears to be faulty. We've had 2 technicians out, and they've done the same thing I have with no determination of what is actually going on. It hasn't happened for almost 2 months. I reached out to Kirk with no response yet. If he doesn't respond tonight or tmrw morning before 7, I'll try again. If not I'll reach out to Greg and see if he has any suggestions. Machine is locked out due to the ram inconsistencies.",
    "attachments": []
  },
