    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "10/30/2024 12:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 10/01/24  5:32:05 AM: Turned power off. Removed cover on pedestal. Removed all buttons/switches and harness. Removed overlay and cleaned all existing glue off. Replaced with new. Plugged in harness and put back all buttons/switches. Put cover back on pedestal. Turned power on and calibrated machine. Checked all buttons and everything is working good.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "192",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 192",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #44 (WC 2018)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "15212",
    "date_notified": "03/31/2025",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "Operator was running machine after 90pcs the machine came down too hard and would have blown dies if the operator wasn't paying attention. Operator tried to just take off the bend and adjust the pinch point but it wouldn't adjust. He powered the machine down and started it back up, after that the machine is back to normal and we lowered the tonnage just in case. (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Closed Without Action",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "1",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "03/31/2025 09:30 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 06/30/25  7:02:55 AM: Adding this to the existing other work order on this machine. | Preston Ellexson - 03/31/25  8:17:26 AM: Within 20 parts after speaking with Jim, it did the same thing. He just left the machine where it was at in the bend so I could look at it. I went ahead and checked the torque on the ways clamps. The outsides were right at the limit, but the insides were a little under. I went ahead and set all to 20 ft.lbs. Some were below 15 when I walked up. Watched Jim run 20-30 parts after adjusting. After making a slight bend adjustment after the re-torque, the ram is holding the bend value now. I just told Jim to holler at me or Shacole if it changed at all. I'll monitor for a few days and close out if nothing changes.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "192",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 192",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #44 (WC 2018)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "15957",
    "date_notified": "06/04/2025",
    "urgency": "3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",
    "problem": "operator says the motor will shut off when hes running, he has to keep his electrical cabinet door open cause it will overheat, and he is shutting it down on lunch to give it time to cool down (Preston is aware of the issue and is looking into it)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "6",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "06/16/2025 02:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 07/02/25  8:20:02 AM: Jim swapped machines so I could really look into this. Ran machine for a bit. Adjusted the torque on all way clamps. They were a little high. I set them to 17-18 ft lbs. I was getting just a bit of heat with this torque setting when operating the ram. This is normal for slight heat. If you can't hold your hand on it because of the heat, the torque is too high and it's causing too much friction. Oiled backgauge ballscrew. Turned machine off and opened electrical cabinet. Tightened every screw in the cabinet. Some were pretty loose. After inspecting the main circuit board, I believe some of the problems are due to the age and wear of it. All valve relays are slightly burned on the board. There are multiple capacitors that have discoloration and slight warping. Swapped out the board with a new one. Got everything hooked up. Double checked all connections in cabinet again. Turned machine on and reset pedestal parameters. Made a quick program to dry run and test machine. I cycled the machine 500-600 times with no problems at all. That only took 30 minutes, but was enough to get everything warmed up to operating temp. I put the thermal overload in manual rest mode to test if it was possibly starting to fail. Let him start running again. I have followed up with him, and he hasn't had any issues since. The tonnage monitor doesn't stay at 0 when ram is still. It might go to 1 ton or 4, but this doesn't affect any operation or safety feature on the machine. No other issues at all. This has been running good for 2 weeks. I am closing this out. I left the thermal overload in manual reset. If it trips they will have to call maintenance, and at that point I'll get a temp read on it if it trips.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "192",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 192",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #44 (WC 2018)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "17059",
    "date_notified": "09/23/2025",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "machine throwing an error with the back gauge with the light curtains",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "3",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "11/05/2025 09:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 11/05/25  6:55:00 AM: 10/24 I got the processor swapped out. Checked parameters prior to changing just in case something needed adjusting. Ran the boot-up sd card and put in the new run sd card as advised per documentation by THCO. When we started running, we were getting an overspeed error on the LaserSafe system. Got with Loris and he said this is typical depending on the setup. He said we could adjust the crawl speed in the parameters. We didn't have to make any adjustments on it though. Jim read the operators manual and changed the way he did his light curtain setup. After adjusting his setup, the machine is running good with no issues. The HMI functions a little different than the older version Jim was used to. Merritt was on the machine the next week. He had issues from the start. I had Jim show him the difference in the setup, and we didn't have any more issues out of it. Machine is running good after adapting our setup. We are still in need of repairing the ways clamps due to age. That affects the machine most on Monday after sitting over the weekend. I am working on quoting and scheduling that repair with Capital. No more issues on this machine. I'll have Shacole put in a new work order when I receive the parts for the mentioned repair. | Preston Ellexson - 10/17/25 11:41:49 AM: We have been waiting for this machine to be available per production scheduling. Shacole is thinking sometime early next week when Jim finishes this run of parts. | Preston Ellexson - 09/26/25  7:43:03 AM: Loris(THCO) and the LazerSafe engineer both agree the processor needs to be replaced. I got a quote from Jeff(THCO) yesterday and the PO got sent this morning. Jeff said he'd try to get it shipped today UPS ground. When it arrives next week, I'll schedule downtime with Shacole to replace this. | Preston Ellexson - 09/25/25  7:37:05 AM: Jim is still running the machine. I told him if it will let him reset when errors happen to just keep running. Loris put in a ticket with LaserSafe and is awaiting a response from them. They are hesitant to have us replace the entire processor due to the cost and question of it completely fixing the problem. I will update Shacole, Jim, and this work order as needed when Loris updates me. | Preston Ellexson - 09/23/25  7:49:20 AM: Got with Jeff and Loris at THCO(Guardomation). They believe the HMI is faulting out causing one of the relays to not to function properly. Contacts are clean on the relays in question. I left the motor running and walked away. It's been running idle for over 30 minutes. I calibrated the machine and did the overrun test. Cycled through the program with no issues. I told Shacole to go ahead and have Jim run it as long as he can. I am still working with Jeff and Loris on resolving this issue. This might have been what's been causing the motor to shut off the past few months we just couldn't catch it. | Preston Ellexson - 09/23/25  5:33:37 AM: I am sending a message to Guardomation at 8 to see what they say about the lazersafe error code. Machine will shut down just sitting idle with the motor running.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
