    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/05/24  9:40:57 AM: (continued)\nMounted the motor/pump shaft cover. Made an aluminum cover for the top of the reservoir and made a solid cork gasket too. Removed motor fan blade cover. Cleaned up and removed all build-up inside. Blew out the motor. Double checked all fittings and turned on. All sounds good and is running smooth. Greased both motor bearings and put cover back on. Greased all zerks on the back of the machine. Machine is cycling good and motor/pump sound good. | Preston Ellexson - 03/05/24  9:36:54 AM: The couplers had shifted on the motor and pump shafts. They slid off far enough where they got in a bind and froze up. Got new ones ordered. Emptied oil reservoir and removed the pump. Everything is still moving good, but there is pretty significant play on the in/out of the pump shaft. Got all put back together when lovejoys arrived. Found the pump seal leaking after I got it all filled up. Removed the oil from the tank and the pump again. Took the pump apart and found the shaft seal was worn by .020-.030. Ordered a new one overnight on 3/1. When part arrived, got the pump put back together and sealed. Put back on machine, filled with oil, cleaned on top of the machine.",
    "attachments": []
  },
