    "completed_datetime": "01/31/2025 12:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 02/04/25 10:26:12 AM: Something in the motor of the hydraulic clamping system is malfunctioning. Swapped the whole power pack out with the new one we still had in maintenance. Got all lines plugged back in, wires hooked up, and filled with fluid. Turned machine on and tested. Everything is working the way it should. I will inspect the other one and see if it's repairable.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "194",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 194",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #42 (WC 2014)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "13298",
    "date_notified": "10/07/2024",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "machine wont ram up or down. we shut the machine down and started back up and it wont move",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "20",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Kirk, Isaac, Matt @ Capital",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "04/10/2025 02:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 04/15/25 11:49:50 AM: Kirk came out and completed the z pulse calibration on the ram. Machine has been running good with no issues since then. | Preston Ellexson - 02/11/25  6:51:32 AM: He replaced the disconnect switch because it completely broke. Machine busted the ram limit switch. Reschedule Matt again after switch arrived. He found the electrical cabinet was mounted a little off when re-installed. Replaced foot pedal cable too. Got machine running. Everything is working pretty good. Having issues with the readout on height of the ram. Thomas @ Capital suggested replacing the ram encoder, or seeing if it needs to be adjusted. I am working on this with Greg now. | Preston Ellexson - 02/11/25  6:48:15 AM: Main motor wasn't starting. Checked motor starter and one leg was reading really high on resistance. Replaced motor starter and thermal overload. Turned machine on and motor was running smooth but very quiet. Didn't have time so setup a visit from Capital. Kirk came out and found the coupler on the pump shaft was split down the middle. He suggested sending the pump out to be inspected and tested due to the amount of torque that would've taken. We sent out and went ahead and got a quote for a new one. Purchased a new one due to lead time on repair of the old one. Isaac came out and installed new pump and got the machine ready to run. Ran into another issue and we had to reschedule another service visit. Matt came out and found a few electrical issues. Had to order parts. Scheduled another service after parts arrived. Replaced main board due to an arc out while he was working.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "194",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 194",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #42 (WC 2014)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "15386",
    "date_notified": "04/15/2025",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "having foot pedal issues, error codes 906/126.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
