    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "04/17/2025 12:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 04/17/25 10:23:50 AM: Followed up with operator today. They have had a few people run it since I looked at it. Machine is running good with no issues. Seems like this might have been a set-up or operator error. For now everything is running good the way it should. | Preston Ellexson - 04/16/25  7:36:55 AM: Checked continuity on the board per documentation. Tested foot pedal and palm buttons. Checked backgauge limit switch. Inspected inside pedestal. Chad was running a skirt where he walks the ram down little by little. This is when they started having issues. When I run it one hit at a time, I have no issues at all. Per documents from Capital, everything on the machine is working the way it should. I suggested maybe trying to run that part different than before. Maybe use a double stop for the ram pinch point to the part. Shut all panels and put everything back together. Machine is good to run. I will leave this work order open til end of week in case we start having more issues on it. | Preston Ellexson - 04/15/25 12:25:14 PM: This just started happening. I turned the power off and checked the foot pedal switches. Made slight adjustment with no change. I am looking at this first thing tomorrow when we get here. Couple things it could be to cause this issue.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
