    "completed_datetime": "03/11/2024 10:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/12/24  6:36:20 AM: Replaced and rewired the motor starter. Double checked everything before testing. Pulled start/stop switch and it runs good. Still troubleshooting. Machine will only run in inch mode. Got back with Kent@BCN and he said that when in inch mode, it bypasses multiple other switches. They do not suggest running the machine in inch mode. Looked over the electrical schematic and checked the rotary switches up top. Found a jumper wire that was missing from switch to switch. Replaced it and tested. Machine is finally running good. All switches are functioning fully. All different modes are functioning the way they should. Got all covers back on and mounted. Removed all maintenance tools/etc from area. Machine is ready to run. | Preston Ellexson - 03/06/24  8:49:28 AM: Pulled start/stop switch, and motor tries to move but only for a second. Quickly pulled start/stop while checking the voltage coming out of the motor starter. Contacts inside motor starter aren't making properly. We are getting good voltage coming in, but dirty voltage coming out. I can manually engage the starter and it works fine with accurate voltage. I got a new motor starter ordered from Grainger that should be here tomorrow. Had Kevin manually engage the motor starter so I could grease both zerks on top and bottom of motor. I am going to put all covers back on today since I know the machine will run good when all needed components are replaced. I will replace the motor starter tomorrow when it arrives. | Preston Ellexson - 03/06/24  8:45:33 AM: Got motor here and it all matches the existing motor. Got installed, wired, and flywheel belts attached. After double checking everything, I went to start machine. Nothing is happening so back to troubleshooting. Found the input module on the start/stop switch was fried internally. Also found a run bulb that was burnt. Ordered module from Radwell and picked up a bulb from Batteries+Bulbs. I am still having issues though. Got with Ben@BCN and he got me with one of the control engineers, Kent. Spoke with Kent and he gave me schematic information. I found the clutch pressure switch wasn't engaging. Got it working and I now have all voltage where needed prior to start/stop switch. | Preston Ellexson - 02/09/24 12:22:52 PM: Removed flywheel cover and front cover. Inspected machine for any issues. Found none. Bolt came from the die. I ordered replacement bolts and springs for this die yesterday. As I was inspecting, the motor/flywheel locked up and wouldn't spin. Released motor tensioner and removed pulley belts. Motor shaft is locked up. Removed wires from motor and removed from the machine. Separated motor and found the bearings are still spinning. The inside of the motor is so dirty, it locked the rotor up. Got a quote for a new motor from BCN and it was ordered today. It has a 5 day leadtime. I will swap when it arrives.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "213",
