    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 213",
    "equipment_name": "Punch Press, 60 ton (WC 2007)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "12945",
    "date_notified": "09/03/2024",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "small punch came down too hard and locked up (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "4",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "09/03/2024 02:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 09/13/24  4:21:47 AM: Put bolts in place of the existing set screws on the pins. We didn't have long enough set screws. Tightened and had Ken test numerous times. Everything is moving the way it should and nothing is loose. Got covers back on and machine is good to run. | Preston Ellexson - 09/13/24  4:20:12 AM: Checked machine with thermal. Motor was fine. Pulley was around 250 degrees. Removed flywheel cover to inspect. One of the bolts on the quick detachable pulley had worked its way loose. The other two were only finger tight. It was working its way off the shaft. No damage to anything. Got it set and tightened. Adjusted belt tension. While doing this I noticed the top brake friction disc pin was missing. It fell into the the small cover on the bottom. The set screw was missing. Checked the bottom pin. It was in place, but the set screw wasn't tight. The brake friction disc was out of alignment. You can only adjust this while the applying air pressure so the brake releases while the clutch is engaged. Had Ken hold down the palm buttons when I told him to, and keep held. While he applied air pressure, I set the brake friction disc back where it should be and put the brake friction disc pin in place.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
