    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "03/10/2025 06:30 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/10/25  4:24:09 AM: These light curtains have been giving us issues more recently. I believe it is because they are mounted directly on a machine that created tonnage. I'm getting with Shacole on mounting the control panel on a post underneath the machine electrical cabinet.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "213",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 213",
    "equipment_name": "Punch Press, 60 ton (WC 2007)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "15614",
    "date_notified": "05/02/2025",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "operator noticed a brake pad fell out of the machine and went and informed Preston.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "3",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "05/02/2025 01:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 05/08/25  8:03:02 AM: Put a jam nut of the brake friction disk pin. Got all back together and tight. Put cover on and had operators check the visual inspection window to ensure they knew what to look for. Everything is good. Removed lock out tag and machine is ready to run. | Preston Ellexson - 05/08/25  8:01:07 AM: Locked machine out. Removed side cover. Found another clutch lining that broke. After inspecting, only 2 linings broke and came off. The reason is because the brake friction disk pin was not in place and fell out. The retainer screw that holds it in place slightly came loose and the pin worked its way out of place. When this happens, the clutch linings don't stay stationary. It shifts every time the palm buttons are engaged and start shifting. I'm not too worried about getting back running even with the 2 linings missing. All the rest are there, and we aren't missing any brake linings. Removed the pin and painted the end yellow. Cut a hole out of the cover so I could put a plexiglas cover window. Got hole cut and cover made. Put bolt and lock nut through so you can swivel it, but it stays covered. Shacole updated the machine checklist to see if the pin is sticking out moving forward. To put the brake friction disk pin in, you have to hold the palm buttons to engage the clutch so it releases from the brake linings and insert it while the operator is holding the buttons. Turned machine off and locked back out.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
