    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "06/04/2024 06:30 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 06/04/24  4:26:39 AM: Swapped out 4 dies with all new springs, and u-clips. Replaced the worst top plates with the new ones we had. We didn't buy enough to replace all. Greased all spring locations before rebuilding. Got everything back together and functional. Sent to Shacole. We are short springs for repairing one die, so it'll stay in maintenance. I got these done a few weeks ago. Shacole let me know they are already having issues with one. I looked at it and there are already multiple springs not working now. Same issue as before. The hook is bending and coming apart from the u-clip which drops the spring. Die has to be taken all the way apart at that plate if any spring is to be repaired. I am getting with Paul on this to see if we want to keep putting money into these or find another option. | Preston Ellexson - 09/18/23 12:11:02 PM: These dies have kept breaking, so through Aaron @ Capital, we sent them back to Wilson. They gave us a quote to replace all bad parts, and it was over $5000. We are having them sent back and I'll order the repair parts to fix all springs and hardware inside all the new bottom black dies. | Preston Ellexson - 05/04/23 11:09:00 AM: Ordered parts today to be sent overnight. | Preston Ellexson - 04/21/23 12:07:28 PM: Got with Shacole on this. I brought die to maintenance. Should be able to replace the spring that is broken or faulty.",
    "attachments": []
  },
