    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 09/23/22  7:49:11 AM: This is linked with the work on the previous work order that was just completed. | Preston Ellexson - 08/18/22  6:27:22 AM: Manually engaged valve and got ram to drop a little. Manually engaged the other like valve and it shifted really hard. As Chad held the pedal, I was hearing something like an air leak or hissing. Checked the speed control, and it was wide open. We closed, then opened 1 1/4 turns and the sound went away. He re-calibrated and everything is working good now. I don't know if we have a valve sticking, or if it was just due to the high pressure bypassing causing issues. I will monitor for a few days.",
