    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 02/11/25  7:09:16 AM: Operator accidentally dropped a die through the machine and it tore the cable and wires out of the motor encoder. Tried using butt connectors to tie back together with no luck. Took over a month to find a solution due to AccurPress not selling any of those components anymore. Had a tech here to work on our big punch press and he said he had some used parts. Bought a used drive/motor/cables from him. Swapped the motor out and used new cables from Capital we ordered. There is a battery procedure to follow from Capital. You have to reset drive errors, calibrate the drives manually and a handful of other things. Got this all done and turned machine on. Calibrated with no issues. Machine is running good.",
    "attachments": []
  },
