    "completed_datetime": "02/12/2025 02:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 02/12/25 12:06:02 PM: Turned machine on, calibrated, and moved x-axis all the way in. Turned machine off and locked out. Removed top cover on backgauge. Took the right(from operators view) finger assembly apart so I could remove the cover panel completely. Bearings are all good. Checked motor brushes on both motors for comparison. They all are similar and not in need of replacing. Removed the right side motor. Belt spins free with no issues once removed. Motor shaft was locked up. Broke free easily with pliers and it was very squeaky. Took motor apart and saw the inner magnets were broken. Sent email to Capital for replacement motor.",
    "attachments": []
