    "completed_datetime": "07/25/2025 01:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 07/28/25  4:41:22 AM: Machine was randomly not moving the backgauge immediately every step change. It would say request backgauge move to target and just wait. Not sure if it made a difference, but if you hit the pedal again, it would move and continue the program. Tried getting a recording to send to Kirk. After looking at the program, I realized the top, slow, and bend were not setup right. The top was lower than the slow and the bend. Not sure how the machine was even running like this without erroring out. Got this all set back right and let Keith run. Every time I tried to record him run a part, the machine would run as it should with no issues. After being over here and it being so inconsistent, I just stopped by every hour and asked him how it was running. He ran for the remainder of the day, Thursday, and Friday with no issues. Originally Chad checked the program and didn't find any issues that he thought would cause this. The change might have been made before or after. It might not have anything to do with the issue he was having. I think it was a programming issue, but no way to be sure of that. Closing out with no action. I will monitor occasionally this week.",
    "attachments": []
  },
