    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "06/05/2026 07:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 06/05/26  5:23:50 AM: Ran some conduit from the junction above where BP#46 used to sit. Put a single gang outlet and a switch as low as I could. It is a little high because there are multiple obstructions on the beam otherwise. The existing 120V power wire was already being used. The old machine wires were 8awg. I tied a 10awg wire on from the breaker side and pulled it through. I could've just used that wire, but it's approximately 140'. There are still 2 wires of 8awg not being used. I left them in case I need to do something else in the future. I'm saving the wire I removed. Got all tied in except breaker. Removed the fan from where the nitrogen generator system used to set. Used an existing fan mount I had already made. Got the mount and fan in place as low as I could. Adjusted the fan to the operator as well. Put a new breaker in, labeled it, and tested power. Everything is good and the fan works as it should. | Preston Ellexson - 05/06/26  6:38:48 AM: I will have to do a short power run and come up with a bracket for the location. I will get this started on this next week.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1545",
