    "completed_datetime": "07/23/2026 09:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 08/12/26  5:12:09 AM: Removed the die from the machine. Brought to maintenance to separate. Got decking off and parts removed. Inspected die for any issues. Everything looks good. Put it back together and got back in the machine. Tested parts with no issues. Die is good to run.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1545",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1545",
    "equipment_name": "Press Brake #56 (WC 2017)",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "20322",
    "date_notified": "08/11/2026",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "Machine stopped and machine will not turn off or estop  (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Pending",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "8",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Jason@Capital",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "08/25/2026 10:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 08/25/26  7:39:56 AM: Jason@Capital Machine came out 8/19 end of day and back first thing 8/20. After working with the factory and with Kevin, they believe the issue is the safety valve and the relief valve. We placed the order yesterday and asked for overnight delivery. I am getting with shipping to let them know to be on the lookout. I will get these swapped out as soon as they arrive and go from there. Jason let me know the electrical schematic I had wasn't 100% accurate. They sent a different revision when they emailed me. He is going to send the right one. | Preston Ellexson - 08/19/26  8:26:22 AM: We will have a technician here tomorrow to troubleshoot this machine. I've got it locked back out. Scott is printing the electrical schematic for me so I can keep a copy in the machine. | Preston Ellexson - 08/12/26 11:34:23 AM: Working on this. At first, this was a different issue. They might be linked, but I haven't investigated far enough. The estop wasn't stopping the motor, and neither was the back gate switch. I cycled the machine power and this issue resolved and everything was turning on and off as it should. Then the hydraulic clamping wouldn't turn on. I had the estop issue happen twice more in between troubleshooting. Hydraulic clamping hasn't worked at all. Got with Kevin @ Capital on this. He is putting in a work order since I'm off for 2 days. I'll coordinate when I return on repairs or continuing with troubleshooting.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
