    "problem": "the die is having issues not sitting flat one side is down more than the other. (Preston is looking at it)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "1",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "05/06/2024 11:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 05/09/24 10:12:32 AM: Got tangs made from Sherman Machine. Had to slot out the tang on the die side. Scott did the math of how much the 2 inner shoulder bolts were moving. He determined we needed at least .085 removed from the tang. I took off a .100 slot where both shoulder bolts ride down. Put die all back together and had Jim test it. He said everything looked good with no issues. I have 2 spare tangs that were made to fit this too. I'll keep them in maintenance. | Preston Ellexson - 04/24/24  7:57:02 AM: Took the die apart and inspected. Die tang was bent again at almost all of the bolt holes. One of the two shoulder bolts that holds the forming section was broken. Took everything off of the die and had Scott take it to Sherman Machine. They are going to machine the die tang opening on the bottom to parallel it and get a tight fit. They are going to make t shaped tangs so they will mount better to the bottom of the die, but still fit in the bed rail. Job is said to be completed by 4/29. When it's completed and delivered I'll put it all back together. First run they have I'll watch it to ensure it's working safe and making a good part.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1550",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1550",
    "equipment_name": "Die Towel Tray Forming #16",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "16029",
    "date_notified": "06/09/2025",
    "urgency": "3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",
    "problem": "pin in the die needs to be looked at, Preston is aware. Die will be taken back to maintenance when we are done running what we need",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "4",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Ken/Jimmie",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "06/17/2025 03:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 06/23/25  8:21:52 AM: Had Ken help me separate the die 6/13 before the week was over. Checked springs and one was curled up around a coil. We don't have any here. Found on McMaster and sent to Paul to order. Parts got ordered 6/16 and delivered on 6/17. We have extra on hand. Guide posts and bushings have fairly bad wear damage but are still usable. I cleaned the guide posts with fine emory cloth. I'm going to get a quote for a new set of posts and bushings. I'm going to order longer guide posts if possible too. Cleaned top and bottom die. Put new springs under locators and put bottom die back together. Got all posts and bushings mounted back on and greased. Had Jimmie help me put die back together. Went together much easier than it did taking it apart. Let Shacole know to be present when running since I'll be on vacation. Die ran with no issues. She sent me measurements of the amount of stroke on the die so I can determine guide post length. Everything is good right now. I will send for a quote and have Paul order replacement parts.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1550",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1550",
    "equipment_name": "Die Towel Tray Forming #16",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "16993",
    "date_notified": "09/15/2025",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "part hung up in die from running it paper down",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "1",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
