    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "09/15/2025 09:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 09/17/25  4:04:58 AM: Tried removing the part with the die separated in the machine. Couldn't get it out. Had operator remove die and bring to maintenance. Separated the top an bottom. Used c-clamps to put tension on the stripper plate. Removed part while the hem tooling had space inside. Got part out. No damage was done to the die at all. Put back together and sent back to punch press.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1550",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1550",
    "equipment_name": "Die Towel Tray Forming #16",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "17405",
    "date_notified": "10/22/2025",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "the locator for the first operation die is stuck down",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "1.5",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "10/22/2025 12:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 10/23/25  4:13:19 AM: Left the top half of the die in the machine. Marked the bottom half on machine bed. Removed bottom half and took to maintenance. Separated die. Springs are still good. The locator was in a jam. Removed both locators and ran on a wire wheel. Used drill and wire brush on the ID of the die locator holes. Cleaned inside of the die while apart. Tested locators and both are functioning with ease. Took back to the machine and had Ken help. Lined up as close as possible and got the top die almost touching the guide posts. Manually adjusted the height down around an inch so the dies were fully seated. Tightened down bottom die. Adjusted machine height back up to the original height. Had him test a part. We went a little too high. After adjusting down twice, the parts look good and are ready to run. Locators are working good.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1551",
