    "comments": "Joshua Patton - 02/29/24  7:35:56 AM: I broke the draw bar for mill Yesterday I ordered new one yesterday from McMaster-Carr it should bee here today when it arrives finishing this die will be my top priority | Joshua Patton - 02/23/24  4:36:29 AM: spoke with Shacole she is going to let me know when the plate is here  and I will get it welded, I have the Die in the maintenance shop",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1551",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1551",
    "equipment_name": "Die Towel Tray Hem/Flat #20",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "14347",
    "date_notified": "01/14/2025",
    "urgency": "2. General Maint - High Priority",
    "problem": "guide pins is bent",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "2700",
    "labor_time": "2",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/H&O Die Supply",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "02/03/2025 06:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 02/05/25  7:49:40 AM: I replaced the guide pins, but had a very hard time get the dies back together. Got with Kevin @ H&O Die Supply. He got with Lonestar, their internal die shop. We got a hot shot delivery to get the die there. Took 1 1/2 weeks. They found issues with top and bottom dies. Re-surfaced both due to them being crowned slightly. Bored out the bushing and guide pin holes due to wear. Installed bigger guide pins and bushings. Added mounts to the guide bushing. Tested die with no issues. We set up 2/3 and ran with no issues.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1551",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1551",
    "equipment_name": "Die Towel Tray Hem/Flat #20",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "17870",
    "date_notified": "12/09/2025",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "position pin spring is broke and will need to be replaced (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "1.5",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "12/18/2025 12:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 12/18/25 10:27:08 AM: Separated the die in maintenance. Removed the bottom part of the die from the plate. Springs are both still good. One locator is still wanting to get stuck. They are measuring around .497. It's a .500 hole. One is a little harder to push in and out as the other. I used a .501 reamer to clean the hole from both sides. Locator slides in and out easy now without binding. Cleaned die and removed all oil. Put white lithium grease on the guides and guide posts. Put top die back on bottom die and got it set. I let Shacole know the die was ready for production. It is in the die rack. | Preston Ellexson - 12/10/25  4:33:06 AM: Die is in maintenance. Got with Shacole, and I will repair this first thing 12/15 next week.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1551",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1551",
    "equipment_name": "Die Towel Tray Hem/Flat #20",
    "department": "Fabrication",
    "wo_id": "20686",
    "date_notified": "09/14/2026",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "The locator pin in the bottom die is stuck down. (Preston is aware)",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "3",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "09/23/2026 09:30 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 09/23/26  7:14:39 AM: Still having slight issues with this. It is happening more frequently. Will ordered a few different conical springs for the locator pins. He said just keep doing what I've been doing to repair and get running until the new die sets get approved. | Preston Ellexson - 09/14/26 10:03:25 AM: Operator came back in an hour and had the same issue. I hooked up a power drill and cleaned the hole with a .501 straight reamer. Cleaned the bottom of the locator pin with a flat file. Put locator back in the die and tested manually. Pin is moving freely. Put the spring back in, set the bottom plate, and tightened as needed. Tested the machine a few times. Die is working well. I let Shacole know this will eventually get to a point where it won't function properly. No way of knowing when it will get to that point. She is letting Paul know so we can get feedback on the die/machine update they've been working on. I am leaving this work order open until the end of the week to monitor. | Preston Ellexson - 09/14/26  9:53:44 AM: Put in a die block and removed the bottom plate. Cleaned up the locator opening and put back together. Tightened bottom plate as needed for alignment. Ran machine and it is working good.",
    "attachments": []
  },
