    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "07/31/2026 08:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 08/07/26  7:52:10 AM: Replaced the relay when they arrived. Still having issues with the water level. Cleaned some build up out of the fill side with the sensor. I checked all settings for the water height. I made numerous adjustments on the levels. Low Low, Low, Set Point, High, and High High. After slowly adjusting these while running, I found a good place to set them at. I let Shacole know how to view them and what they were set at. There is more of a window from low to high now in comparison to what the actual readout is of the water level. | Preston Ellexson - 07/30/26  8:07:09 AM: Checked everything inside the electrical cabinet. The PLC isn't getting consistent power. I could wiggle some wires and get it to work off and on. Checked every wire inside. Tightened all to verify. Still same issue. Checked the slim relays. The K1 relay NC contacts are faulty inside. I sent a quote request to Radwell. Grainger has different brand, so I was hesitant. Found some aftermarket ones on Amazon that will deliver sometime today. If I don't hear anything from Radwell today, I'll reach out to a different contact person there. I'll get on this today if the order arrives while I'm here.",
    "attachments": []
  },
